job-name-director = Site Director
job-description-director = Direct supervisor of the Site and its' administration staff, with full access. to ensure the speedy completion of the tasks set by the regional administration. Class A
job-name-scientific-service-director = Research and Development Director
job-description-scientific-service-director = Head of the site's Research and Development division, regulating its work and often responsible for completing goals set by regional administration staff. The second most important person in the site. CLASS A
job-name-security-commander = Security Commander
job-description-security-commander = The Head of Security. Directly responsible for the safety and security of all Zones - EZ and HCS. He has full access throughout the site, as well as special equipment to assist in his work. The third most important person in the site. CLASS B
job-name-chief-technical-specialist = Chief Technical Specialist
job-description-chief-technical-specialist = The chief technician of the site, responsible for fixing things and keeping the lights on. The fourth most important person in the site. CLASS C
job-name-personnel-officer = Personnel Officer
job-description-personnel-officer = The head of Human Resources. Responsible for modifying and replacing identification cards, and also monitors the quality of the food and sanitation of the site. The fifth most important person in the site. CLASS B
job-name-head-of-medical-sector = Chief Physician
job-description-head-of-medical-sector = The chief physician of the site, responsible for keeping people alive, healthy, and in a state to work. The sixth most important person in the site. CLASS B
job-name-senior-logistics-officer = Quartermaster
job-description-senior-logistics-officer = The chief logistician, responsible for keeping the site supplied. The seventh most important person in the site. CLASS C
job-supervisors-regional-administration = regional administration
job-supervisors-O5-command = the O5 Council
job-supervisors-director = Site Director
